:100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.278,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":27.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"Anteris Technologies Global Corp., a structural heart company, develops and commercializes minimally invasive medical devices to treat heart valve diseases. It offers the DurAVR transcatheter heart valve system, a novel transcatheter aortic valve for the treatment of severe aortic stenosis that is shaped to mimic the performance of a healthy human aortic valve. The company also develops ADAPT anti-calcification tissue, an anti-calcification preparation which transforms xenograft tissue into durable bioscaffolds that are used to mimic human tissue for surgical repair in multiple settings, including aortic valve replacement; and ComASUR delivery system, a physician-developed balloon expandable delivery system that contains a reinforced steerable catheter for a precise deflection through the heart anatomy in a controlled manner to avoid damage to the aorta. Anteris Technologies Global Corp. is based in Toowong, Australia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Wayne Geoffrey Paterson | Vice Chairman & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 174 people. Revenue per employee of $11K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $45K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 152\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Anteris Technologies Global Cor is a small-cap healthcare business with a $555M market cap on $2M of annual revenue.","The company is burning through $80M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -71.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -1286.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 4.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 407% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-21.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 4909% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (72% sell ratio, net $13.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Value